# PCBZ wasm page patch 0012: the editor on a worker-owned OffscreenCanvas, its bundled CJK face,
# the read-only switch and the export guard.
# Why: the page and the chat share the host's one main thread, so the wasm editor must never run
# there (red line a). A dedicated Worker gets the canvas with transferControlToOffscreen(); this
# patch adds the worker-side host that turns that OffscreenCanvas into a wgpu surface (WebGPU, else
# WebGL2), builds the app with a wasm constructor (a worker has no document, CreationContext or
# LocalStorage), and runs one egui pass per call with the page's input JSON (the render server's
# InputEvent vocabulary, copied because that crate is a native binary). egui's repaint request calls
# the page's `pcbzWorkerWake`, so an idle editor still answers a queued host request.
# Chinese project, sheet and net names need a bundled face: the page pushes an OFL subset into
# `pcbcraft_chrome::fonts` before the app is built, and the wasm branch of the CJK fallback uses it
# (desktop still probes its system fonts). `pcbz_host_read_only` turns the running session read-only
# for the licence gate; the save route refuses as well. The three inline export downloads call the
# page's `pcbzOnExport` when it is present, so a host page never produces an unstamped download;
# a plain browser keeps its download UI.
# Files touched: apps/pcbcraft-web/{Cargo.toml, src/main.rs, new src/worker/{mod,input}.rs};
# crates/app/src/{new worker_app.rs, lib.rs module + host_tick read-only + host-mode New/Open guards
# + a keep-alive repaint while a file job runs, host.rs request and host-page flag, the three export
# inline-JS guards, project_files.rs and project_files/web.rs for a larger encode slice on the host
# page}; crates/chrome/src/fonts.rs (bundled wasm face).
# No eframe change: wgpu already accepts SurfaceTarget::OffscreenCanvas; the page's worker calls
# this app's exports instead of eframe's WebRunner.

